<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" align="center" class="tborder" style="border-bottom: 0;">
	<tr class="titlebg">
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="15%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/topic/normal_post.gif" alt="" />
			Author
		</td>
		<td valign="middle" align="left" width="85%" style="padding-left: 6px;">
			Topic: Chapter 3 &nbsp;(Read 121 times)
		</td>
	</tr>
</table>
<table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%" class="bordercolor">
	<tr><td style="padding: 1px 1px 0 1px;">
		<table cellpadding="3" cellspacing="0" border="0" width="100%">
			<tr><td class="windowbg">
				<table width="100%" cellpadding="5" cellspacing="0">
					<tr>
						<td valign="top" width="15%" rowspan="2">
							<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=81" title="View the profile of Phoebie">Phoebie</a></b><br />
							<span class="smalltext">
								Orc Pawn<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/star.gif" alt="*" border="0" /><br />
								Posts: 15<br />
								<br />
								<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/YaBBImages/avatars/blank.gif" alt="" border="0" /><br />
								I'm a llama!<br />
								<br />
								
								
								
								<br />
								<a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?action=profile;u=81"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/icons/profile_sm.gif" alt="View Profile" title="View Profile" border="0" /></a>
								<a href="mailto:brneydmzo@bellsouth.net"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/email_sm.gif" alt="Email" title="Email" border="0" /></a>
							</span>
						</td>
						<td valign="top" width="85%" height="100%">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=117.msg372#msg372"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=117.msg372#msg372">Chapter 3</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b> on:</b> April 10, 2003, 02:00:35 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							The ropes were beginning to cut into her soft white flesh at the wrists and ankles, and she cursed herself over and over again as she faded in and out of her feverish sleep. &nbsp;Her lips were dry and cracked, and she was overwhelmingly thirsty. &nbsp;Her eyes rolled back up into her skull again, tossing her into another frenzied nightmare. &nbsp;She relived the event again and again in her head, wondering how she could have been so foolish as to succumb to the deceptive illusions in this dark place of death.<br /><br />She had only been trying to help, and when she heard the voice of her beloved Aussie crying out her name, she had instantly moved towards his pleading voice, not realizing that she was walking willingly into the arms of the enemy. &nbsp;She had meandered along the slimy stone floor, lifting her robes slightly in hopes that the deep blue silk would not drag along the mucked up floors, and as she deftly jumped across a small pool of bile, she heard the voice of Aussie again.<br /><br />&quot;Cinamini...love...come to me...my wounds...I need you....hurry...hurry...&quot;<br /><br />She looked around frantically, calling his name, the hair on her arms standing on end as a foul chilly breeze passed over her flesh, as if she had stepped through the wandering spirit of something dead. &nbsp;Suddenly spying the crumpled body of her husband in the corner of a dark alley, she could see that he was breathing raggedly, a large gash of dark blood smeared across his forehead, looking almost black against his blue complexion. &nbsp;He raised his head faintly at the sight of her, his hand reaching out towards her, trembling.<br /><br />&quot;Come to me...love...lay your hands on me....my wounds are great...speak your words of health....quickly...&quot;<br /><br />He collapsed again onto the ground with a soft thud as his arm fell to the stones, and screaming, Cinamini had rushed to his side immediately, taking him in her arms, her mind racing quickly to recall the spells that would pull him from his creeping coma of pain and injury. &nbsp;As she stroked his face, looking down upon his pale lips and bleeding head, she felt a wave of horror sweep over her, one so overwhelming she thought she might vomit right there on the spot. &nbsp;Her arms were suddenly not encircling her beloved spouse, but rather the sickly pale flesh of a kiraukel, a doppleganger of the dead, yellow and grinning with a dark rotting mouth, eyes dripping with pus, a hiss of green breath emitting from his nostrils and filling her brain with the stench of decay. &nbsp;Screaming loudly, she had jumped from her crouch and raced along the stone floor, her foot catching in a crevice and tripping her. &nbsp;Her legs became entwined in her heavy skirts and undergarments, and she frantically clawed at the ground trying to take hold of something solid to pull her up to her feet again. &nbsp;As she struggled violently, her arms grew heavy, her movements suddenly slowed and lethargic. &nbsp;She heard the raspy whisper of the kiraukel from close behind her, chanting words of magic that filled her brain with confusion and pain. <br /><br />&quot;Lie sssssstill, pretty one....sssssshh....the pain is only temporary, don't fight it.....rrrrrrrelax.....that's my girl....let my arms embrace your soul.....a bit more now...I need a bit more of you....aaaaaah...yes....&quot;<br /><br />Her mind flickered in and out of reality, swirling downward quickly into a black spiral of confusion, dripping poisonous pain lulling her muscles into apathy, and she fainted finally, breath rasping from her violently as she fell forward onto the stone floor.<br /><br />The kiruakel hobbled up behind her, cackling with glee, large bubbling drops of saliva pouring out of his mouth and spattering the robes of the helpless high elf as he giggled maniacally, dancing around her fallen body. &nbsp;Finally picking her up and slinging her over his shoulder with surprising strength, the minion carried her quickly through the passageways, up the ramps, across the barren stone corridors to the dark rotting room of his Lord. &nbsp;Slinking subserviently to the feet of his awaiting master, he grinned and hissed like a posessed lizard, the eyes of his Master falling upon him at last as he approached.<br /><br />&quot;I am plllleasssed, my feckless fiend. You have done what I wish...and now, I shall give you your ultimate reward.&quot;<br /><br />The kiruakel placed Cinamini at the foot of the throne, bowing and scraping pathetically as he backed away from the throne, his eyes eager for his promised reward, thinking his reward might be the flesh of this mortal, or perhaps, an opportunity to escape this dark realm and haunt the land of the living, feeding on the bodies of the unsuspecting and weak.<br /><br />With the toss of his head and the flick of his hands, the Dark Master shot a bolt of green glowing energy towards the surprised face of the kiruakel. &nbsp;His body began to steam, the flesh peeling from his bones with sickening rapidity, and in seconds all that remained of the sycophant was a shiny pool of melted skin littered with splinters of bone and tooth. <br /><br />That was the last thing she could remember, the hollow deathly grin of Innoruuk staring down at her, paralyzing her with fear. &nbsp;He had carried her to a sturdy wooden post in his chamber and tied her rapidly with ropes that seemed almost alive, they spun around her wrists at his bidding, tightening as she struggled, shooting needles of splintering pain into her flesh as she resisted. &nbsp;Overwhelmed by horror and poisonous aching terror, she had fainted again, her mind lost in a dark corner of her subconscious, clinging to the energies of Tunare, crying out for strength that she knew she must muster to escape.<br /><br />She could hear the rumbling almost growly chants of the Dark One echo in her brain, and she didn't know if she was dreaming, or if it was reality. &nbsp;His voice was deceptively seductive, his words carefully pronounced, heavily accented by the dark lilt of the Teir'Dal dialect, one she had learned secretly long ago when she had fallen in love with the young Necromancer Aussie in the forests of Kithicor when she was a young initiate of Felewithe.<br /><br />&quot;I have great plans for you, sweet one...&quot; She felt a leathery hand slide down her face and her arm, a pointed fingernail tracing a line of red down her exposed ivory flesh. She shuddered with revulsion, trying to pretend she was still asleep, hoping he might leave her alone if he fancied her unconscious. &quot;Your magic is strong, healing pulses from your delicate flesh. I can taste your goodness, it is like a rot in my mouth, one I long to spit out. &nbsp;But your powers to communicate with the Whore of Light are ones I must harness...Tunare must listen to me, once and for all, and if I must sacrifice hundreds of her weak servants to get her attention, then sobeit...&quot; &nbsp;His hand continued down her arm, across her neck, his hands trailing down between her breasts, along the top of her thigh, and back up her stomach again. &nbsp;He placed his hand beneath the left side of her ribcage, his finger feeling like it was pointing directly at her heart, and he cackled loudly, his voice tremoring slightly as he continued. &quot;Aaaah, yes. I know your heart, young one..what you love...who you cherish....you are powerless, your strength grows less with each breath you take. &nbsp;Show me now that which I long to see....where is the Temptress of Growth, the Harlot of Life, the self-proclaimed Goddess of Filth? Show me to her rotting tree...I must see her face once more....tell her of my plans, watch her writhe and twitch when she realizes she can no longer stop me....&quot;<br /><br />Her mind raged against his probing thoughts, pushing him out with all the strength she had left, and he howled in disgust as she quietly whispered words of divine aura, shielding herself with runes of protection, warding him off with quiet chanting prayers. &nbsp;Her strength ebbed, and with a withering hiss, she slipped again into the warm sleepiness of unconsciousness.<br /><br />****<br /><br />Izdain and the other clerics could sense the presence of Cinamini, and with each passing hour her signals were growing weaker, fading in and out, but the clarity of her message remained the same.<br /><br />&quot;Save me....Tunare must be warned....find me quickly....&quot;<br /><br />Izdain wiped his overly-large forehead with his hand, the sweat was cold and clammy in this place, and although he seemed perpetually cold, he sweated like a whore in church. &nbsp;The dark masters of Erudin had warned him when he was young of this place, and now he felt the pain of his responsibility bearing down on him like a crushing boulder.<br /><br />&quot;We must find her, Karadana. She is crying out for us, and I am sure that Aussie can hear her as well, his ability to commune with the arcane must allow him to feel her pain even more than we do.&quot;<br /><br />Karadana stood, her height exceeding six feet, her arms and legs strong and etched with the strength of the tundra, her blonde hair flowing down past her shoulders in a curtain of golden silk, her pretty face now etched with worry for her friend. &nbsp;She whispered to the Tribunal beneath her breath, her hands reaching towards the sky, light flooding her eyes with purple illumination, allowing her to see once again in this place of dark. &nbsp;<br /><br />&quot;Damned place, I can't see jack shit in here. &nbsp;Where is that scaly iksar husband of mine? He said he would be right back.&quot;<br /><br />She stood a bit higher on the wall, surveying the surroundings with her night-blind eyes, and with a frustrated sigh she sank back down to the ground, pulling out her potion bags and evaluating her supplies of ingredients. &nbsp;Deftly shaking the small vials of green and blue and red liquids, she grabbed her mortar and pestle, dropping in several green leafy things and crushing them violently. &nbsp;She poured a vial of oozing green juice into the mortar, and stirring it until it bubbled, she quickly transferred it to another vial and stoppered it up, shaking it again and peering at it closely.<br /><br />&quot;Here, hold this in your pocket, it will ward off the poisons of this place, should you be cursed. I am making them for everyone, please let them know they need to see me if they want to have a way of healing themselves should disaster strike.&quot;<br /><br />Izdain nodded absentmindedly, and shoved the vial deep into the pockets of his robes, feeling the warmth of the still mixing potion flood his thigh with heat. &nbsp;He stood up, determined to find the other clerics and speak to them about Cinamini, perhaps they could form a prayer circle and commune with the Goddess herself, alerting her to the dire situation that was at hand.<br /><br />Out of nowhere, a bright light flashed briefly in the distance. &nbsp;The ears of the adventurers perked up, they recognized the lilting laughter of the wood elf Phoebie. &nbsp;Porting into the zone, the howls of the dead echoed to a crescendo, the good magic was now beginning to compete with the dark forces that ruled this place with each person that entered the walls of this wretched plane. &nbsp;At last, reinforcements had arrived, and none too soon.<br />A wave of relief flooded the guildmembers, voices called out to identify the location of the camp, and finally as if an answer to prayer, the faces of six more brave adventurers peered around the corner.<br /><br />********<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
							<table width="100%" border="0"><tr>
								<td align="left" colspan="2" class="smalltext">
								</td>
							</tr><tr>
								<td align="left" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
								</td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
									<img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/ip.gif" alt="" border="0" /> Logged
								</td>
							</tr></table>
						</td>
					</tr>
				</table>
			</td></tr>
		</table>
	</td></tr>
</table>
